# Parent .gitignore re-included this `.claude/` directory against the
# global `.claude` ignore. Once a directory is re-included, the global
# pattern still matches files inside it as residual; explicitly negate
# the pieces we actually track. hooks/ is tracked by directory rule
# in git-ls-files so no extra entry needed here, but settings.json
# requires its own negation since it's a file directly under .claude/.
!/settings.json
